## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a plugin-based telemetry system with runtime extensibility, backend-agnostic core, and non-blocking emission, which mirrors real-world needs in large distributed systems.

## Key Concepts
- Plugin architecture, dynamic loading, and factories
- Runtime registry mapping names to backends
- Non-blocking I/O via async queues
- Backends with a common Tracer contract

## Code Example
```javascript
interface Tracer {
  emit(event: string, payload: any, ts?: number): void
}
class NoOpTracer implements Tracer { emit() {} }
class RuntimeTracerRegistry {
  private registry = new Map<string, () => Tracer>();
  register(name: string, factory: () => Tracer) { this.registry.set(name, factory); }
  get(name: string): Tracer { const f = this.registry.get(name); return f ? f() : new NoOpTracer(); }
}
```

